!! Configuration

All are plain config tiddlers; edit them in the settings tab or override them in your wiki.

|!Tiddler |!Default |!Meaning |
|`$:/config/rimir/drop-attach/title-filter` |`[<target>addsuffix[/]addsuffix<filename>]` |Title of the new tiddler; first result counts. Variables: `target`, `filename`, `type`, `source`, `size`. A taken title gets `-1`, `-2`, … before the extension |
|`$:/config/rimir/drop-attach/open-filter` |(empty = never) |Runs on each new tiddler; those it keeps open in the story right after the story tiddler you dropped on (or that holds the stream row). `[all[]]` = always. Note: core `is[image]` also matches PDFs; for images only use `[all[]] :filter[get[type]prefix[image/]]` |
|`$:/config/rimir/drop-attach/max-size` |`30` |Size limit per file in MB. Bigger files are skipped with a notice |
|`$:/config/rimir/drop-attach/paste-name` |`[<now YYYY0MM0DD-0hh0mm0ss>addprefix[pasted-]addsuffix[.]addsuffix<ext>]` |File name for pasted files without a real name (screenshots arrive as `image.png`). Variables: `ext`, `type` |
|`$:/config/rimir/drop-attach/extra-types` |Outlook `.msg`, `.7z`, `.odt`, `.ods` |One `<mime type> <.extension>` per line, `#` = comment. Registered as base64 types at startup. ''Restart'' (reload; on a server, restart it) |

!! After-upload actions

Tiddlers tagged <<tag "$:/tags/rimir/drop-attach/action">>, run in tag order once per attached file, right after its tiddler was created. Their text is an action string with these variables:

|!Variable |!Value |
|`new` |Title of the new tiddler |
|`target` |Title of the tiddler (or stream row) it was dropped or pasted on |
|`filename` |File name as dropped (pasted files: from `paste-name`) |
|`type` |Tiddler type, e.g. `application/pdf` |
|`size` |Size in bytes |
|`source` |`drop` or `paste` |

The plugin ships none.

!! Drop targets

Tagged <<tag "$:/tags/rimir/drop-attach/target">>. Shipped: story tiddlers in view mode, sq/streams rows.

|!Field |!Meaning |
|`selector` |CSS selector of the elements that stand for a tiddler (one selector, no comma) |
|`title-attribute` |Attribute of that element holding the title |

The innermost matching element is the target. During a file drag it has the class `da-dragover`.

!! The new tiddler

|!Field |!Value |
|`title` |From `title-filter` |
|`type` |The file's type |
|`text` |The file, base64 |
|`drop-attach.file` |The original file name. Also the marker for extracting |
|`created`, `modified`, `creator`, `modifier` |As for any new tiddler |

!! State

|!Tiddler |!Meaning |
|`$:/temp/rimir/drop-attach/target` |Selected paste target (`text` = title). Not saved |

!! Extracting files

Writes every attachment to `files/` next to the output, points the tiddler at it with `_canonical_uri` and empties its `text`:

```
tiddlywiki <wiki> \
  --save "[has[drop-attach.file]]" "[encodeuricomponent[]addprefix[files/]]" \
  --setfield "[has[drop-attach.file]]" _canonical_uri "$:/plugins/rimir/drop-attach/templates/canonical-uri" text/plain \
  --setfield "[has[drop-attach.file]]" text "" text/plain \
  --render "$:/core/save/all" index.html text/plain
```

`--save` writes the binaries (one file per tiddler, the title URI-encoded). The first `--setfield` renders `$:/plugins/rimir/drop-attach/templates/canonical-uri` (`files/<title, double URI-encoded>`, like the core external-image template) into `_canonical_uri`, the second empties `text`, and `--render` writes the wiki with the changed tiddlers. Copy `index.html` and the `files/` folder together. Narrow the filter to extract only some, e.g. `[has[drop-attach.file]prefix[Projects/]]`.

